   "text": "PREVIOUSLY LOCATED NEAR 7.1S 69.3E IS NOW LOCATED NEAR 7.1S 68.9E, APPROXIMATELY 213 NM WEST OF DIEGO GARCIA. ANIMATED MULTISPECTRAL SATELLITE IMAGERY (MSI) DEPICTS AN INCREASINGLY OBSCURED, CONSOLIDATING LOW-LEVEL CIRCULATION CENTER (LLCC) WITH PERSISTENT CONVECTION BUILDING OVER THE LLCC. A 240255Z SSMIS F16 91 GHZ MICROWAVE IMAGE DEPICTS CURVED, DEEP CONVECTIVE BANDING SLOWLY CONSOLIDATING AROUND THE LLCC TO THE NORTH. A RECENT OBSERVATION AT 111155Z FROM DIEGO GARCIA SHOWS WINDS FROM THE NORTHWEST AT 14 KNOTS WITH AN MSLP OF 1011 MB. ENVIRONMENTAL ANALYSIS REVEALS A MODERATELY FAVORABLE ENVIRONMENT FOR DEVELOPMENT WITH HIGH VERTICAL WIND SHEAR (VWS) OF 20-25 KNOTS, STRONG RADIAL UPPER-LEVEL OUTFLOW, AND WARM SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES (SST) OF 28-29",
